  speakerName: Kyros
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'As the sun sets and the streetlamps begin to glow, the greeting
    changes with the time of day.

    In Ilokano, ''naimbag a rabii'' means ''good
    evening.''

    Use it when greeting someone in the evening.

    Now, try saying
    ''naimbag a rabii'' yourself.'
